WEBVTT

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:08.464
Ambassador's Log,
Stardate 53263.2.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.702
Though helpful
during my negotiations

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.039
on the Kesat homeworld,

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:15.104
Commander Tuvok certainly hasn't
been the most sociable

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.876
of travel companions.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.315
Mr. Neelix.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:20.148
Sorry.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:30.426
How about a game of "Species,
Starship or Anomaly"?

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.624
Surely you could find
something more productive

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.257
to occupy your time.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.494
Come on, Tuvok.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.160
It'll be fun.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.899
You think of something...
species, anomaly or starship...

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.066
and I have 15 questions
to guess what it is.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.268
Come on, come on,
come on, come on.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:46.904
I would prefer
some peace and quiet.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.112
How about a riddle?

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.241
Mr. Neelix.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.285
Come on!

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.583
Ha. It'll be fun.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.782
I have no desire for fun.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.222
Okay, forget fun.

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:02.284
A good riddle can
stimulate the mind.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.331
Now, no self-respecting
Vulcan can say no to that.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:07.792
Very well.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.164
One riddle.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.897
Okay, here goes.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.202
A lone Ensign finds
himself stranded

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:18.904
on a Class-L planetoid
with no rations.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:22.573
His only possession...
a calendar.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.948
When Starfleet finds
him 12 months later,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.680
he's in perfect health.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:31.383
Why didn't he starve to death?

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.551
It is a theoretical possibility

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:38.063
that such planetoids contain
hot water springs,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:41.066
which could sustain the man
for several weeks.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.965
Ooh, but not for a whole year.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.071
I concur.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.230
Logic dictates

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.240
that the Ensign
in question would perish.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.275
Aha!

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.611
Ha! I stumped you.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.943
As a matter of fact,

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.381
he not only survived,
but his belly was full.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.852
Why? Because he feasted
on "dates" from the calendar.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.584
Your answer is merely wordplay.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.057
It has no basis in reality.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.594
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.821
Where are you going?

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.423
To find some peace and quiet.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.229
Have fun.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.748
Tuvok to Neelix.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.655
Miss me already, Commander?

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:42.217
Did you activate
the aft tactical station?

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.353
No.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.659
Why?

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.132
There appears to be
a download in progress.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.294
That's odd.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.464
I'm detecting
anomalous readings.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.599
What sort of readings?

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.235
I'm not certain, but I believe

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.710
it's a cloaking frequency
that consists...

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.409
Commander?

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.850
Tuvok!

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:13.917
Delta Flyer to Voyager.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.119
Mayday!

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:23.035
Tuvok, what happened?

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.209
Report.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.480
He's in neuroleptic shock.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.749
I'll need another
20 milligrams of synaptizine.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.222
I'll get it.

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.722
It's not working.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:33.891
I'll need to try
direct cortical stimulation.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.900
Initiate a neurostatic pulse
on my mark.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.026
Right.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:39.695
Now!

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:43.299
Again!

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:53.650
His vital signs have stabilized
for the moment, anyway.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.814
But he suffered severe
neurological trauma.

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.224
Do you know what caused it?

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:01.624
Some kind of alien weapon.

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:04.561
By the time I reached Tuvok,

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.120
whoever had attacked him
was gone.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:07.894
What about
the surrounding space?

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.901
Any indication
of cloaked vessels?

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:12.027
Between trying to tend
to the Commander

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:14.471
and piloting the Flyer,
I had my hands full.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.906
I... I didn't think
to scan for cloaked ships.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:17.908
I'm sorry.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.443
You saved Tuvok's life, Neelix.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:21.207
You have nothing
to be sorry about.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.645
How do you plan to treat him?

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:25.582
I won't know until I've run
a series of neurological scans.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:26.845
But it would certainly help

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.546
to know something
about the weapon.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:32.284
Neelix, these Kesat
you were negotiating with...

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.918
any reason to believe they
might know something about this?

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:37.155
It couldn't hurt to ask.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.824
Time to reopen
diplomatic channels.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:49.732
Deputy Investigator Naroq,
Kesat Security.

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:52.141
Captain Janeway,
Commander Chakotay,

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.143
Ambassador Neelix.

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:54.474
You've done your homework.

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:56.481
I familiarized myself
with the facts

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:57.743
on the way here.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:06:59.614
We're hoping you can help us
shed some light

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.152
on what happened to our crewman.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.346
I believe I can.

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:04.686
Based on the information
you provided,

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:07.487
it is my opinion that he was
a victim of the Ba'Neth.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.720
I've never heard of them.

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:09.989
I'm not surprised.

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:12.292
In my language, their name
means "shadow people."

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:15.493
They're a species obsessed
with concealing their identity...

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.695
extremely paranoid
and xenophobic.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.000
Well, that explains
their cloaking technology.

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.505
It's my belief

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.064
they've been responsible
for several

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.837
unexplained attacks
similar to this one.

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.344
Why wasn't I warned about them

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:28.573
during my negotiations
with your government?

00:07:28.648 --> 00:07:30.479
Because my government's
official position

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.245
is that
the Ba'Neth do not exist.

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:34.047
Most people think
they're a myth.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.417
There's nothing mythical

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:37.251
about what happened
to Mr. Tuvok.

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:39.257
Why is your government
so skeptical?

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:40.690
Because there have been

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.625
so few encounters
with the Ba'Neth.

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:45.095
And, well, no one's ever
actually seen one.

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:48.600
How many encounters
are we talking about exactly?

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:51.865
Before this incident, 12.

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:55.396
I guess we're lucky 13.

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:56.942
You're lucky
I gave my supervisor

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:58.909
two bottles of Kesatian ale
to get this assignment.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.639
Any other inspector would have
simply attributed

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:04.240
Commander Tuvok's injuries
to "unexplained phenomena."

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:06.182
No offense, Mr. Naroq,

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:10.882
but what makes you so sure
the Ba'Neth aren't just a myth?

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.891
This incident fits
the pattern, Captain.

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:14.788
All of the alleged encounters

00:08:14.861 --> 00:08:17.421
have occurred aboard vessels
foreign to this sector.

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.897
I believe they've been
attempts by the Ba'Neth

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:22.227
to assess the technology
of new arrivals.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:25.429
They were trying to
download tactical data.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:27.905
And Commander Tuvok suffered
severe neural damage.

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:30.568
That's also consistent
with previous attacks.

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:32.270
The Ba'Neth were making sure

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:34.514
he would not tell anyone
what he saw.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:38.744
Maybe that's why
Tuvok's tricorder was destroyed.

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:40.786
They didn't want us to see

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:43.413
the cloaking frequency
he'd found.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.787
He found a cloaking frequency?

00:08:45.858 --> 00:08:47.485
Apparently.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.323
Captain, I don't blame you

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:52.091
for finding my theories
a bit eccentric.

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:53.358
I'm used to it.

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:55.923
It's why I'm still
a deputy investigator.

00:08:56.002 --> 00:08:59.267
But I've brought equipment
to help your investigation.

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.465
Let me examine Commander Tuvok

00:09:01.541 --> 00:09:03.805
and run scans on the vessel
where he was attacked.

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:07.312
I may finally be able
to prove my theories.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.779
With all due respect,

00:09:08.848 --> 00:09:12.181
we're more interested
in saving Tuvok's life.

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:16.244
If we work together,
maybe we can do both.

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:21.426
His cognitive, memory
and logic centers

00:09:21.494 --> 00:09:23.257
have all been severely damaged.

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:26.127
But he still has brain activity,
which is more than I can say

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:27.688
for any of the previous victims.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:29.826
Vulcan neural tissue
is extremely resilient.

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:32.302
I have no doubt that a brain
from a lesser species

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.430
would not have survived.

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:36.805
If you could only tell us
what you saw, Mr. Tuvok.

00:09:36.876 --> 00:09:39.640
I don't think we'll be hearing
from him anytime soon.

00:09:39.712 --> 00:09:40.838
Keep working.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:44.178
I'll let you know if we find
anything that might help.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.083
I'll take you to see
where the attack occurred.

00:09:59.031 --> 00:10:01.158
Something I can do
for you, Mr. Neelix?

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:02.393
I want to help.

00:10:02.468 --> 00:10:05.062
Unless you have a degree
in Vulcan neurobiology

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:08.595
that I'm not aware of,
there's nothing you can do.

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:10.869
There must be something.

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:13.036
My advice is to return
to your quarters

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:14.443
and get some rest.

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:17.175
There's no way that I'm going
to be able to sleep

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:19.979
knowing that Tuvok is
lying here like this.

00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:27.949
There have been rare cases

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:31.929
in which comatose patients
responded to external stimuli:

00:10:31.998 --> 00:10:34.660
Aromas, touch, voices.

00:10:34.734 --> 00:10:38.830
So... you're saying
that if I stay here

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:40.963
and, and try to talk to Tuvok,
I might be able

00:10:41.073 --> 00:10:42.700
to provoke some sort
of response.

00:10:42.775 --> 00:10:47.838
If anyone can provoke Tuvok,
Mr. Neelix, it's you.

00:10:56.922 --> 00:10:57.946
Good morning, Tuvok!

00:10:58.024 --> 00:11:00.584
I brought you a few more
items from your quarters

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.457
to help liven up Sick Bay.

00:11:02.528 --> 00:11:04.587
Your kal-toh game,

00:11:04.664 --> 00:11:07.929
in case you decide
you're ready for a match.

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:09.534
Oh, and I also thought

00:11:09.602 --> 00:11:11.797
that you might enjoy
a recitation

00:11:11.871 --> 00:11:14.271
of that classic
proto-Vulcan drama,

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.171
Clash on the Fire Plains.

00:11:16.242 --> 00:11:20.201
I'll be performing
all 23 parts myself.

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:23.806
Uh, I also brought
you some flowers

00:11:23.883 --> 00:11:25.942
from Airponics Bay.

00:11:26.018 --> 00:11:28.418
Oh, that's fragrant, isn't it?

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:36.652
Uh, perhaps you'd enjoy
some Vulcan incense.

00:11:42.501 --> 00:11:44.901
Now, how about some music?

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:54.436
Computer, access Vulcan audio
file, selection 56-Alpha.

00:12:02.621 --> 00:12:06.182
Mr. Neelix, what is
that dreadful noise?

00:12:06.258 --> 00:12:09.193
The Chants of the Monks
of T'Panit.

00:12:09.261 --> 00:12:11.195
Personally, I think
it's dreadful, too,

00:12:11.263 --> 00:12:12.924
but it's one
of Tuvok's favorites.

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:14.862
I appreciate your efforts,
Mr. Neelix,

00:12:14.934 --> 00:12:17.562
but I'm trying to analyze
his latest neurological scans

00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:21.163
and this music
is very distracting.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:23.834
You said I was supposed
to stimulate his senses.

00:12:23.909 --> 00:12:27.037
I said stimulate them, Mr.
Neelix, not annihilate them.

00:12:27.113 --> 00:12:29.343
Computer, pause music.

00:12:29.415 --> 00:12:31.144
Thank you.

00:12:36.555 --> 00:12:38.819
Doctor.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.191
Tuvok!

00:12:44.697 --> 00:12:46.528
You've had an accident.

00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:48.066
You're in Sick Bay.

00:12:50.035 --> 00:12:53.300
Relax, Commander,
I only want to scan you.

00:12:53.372 --> 00:12:54.964
Don't worry, Tuvok.

00:12:55.107 --> 00:12:57.337
He's only trying to help you.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.844
It's only a tricorder.

00:13:05.918 --> 00:13:07.579
See?

00:13:07.653 --> 00:13:10.349
L-it won't hurt you.

00:13:11.657 --> 00:13:12.817
Now try it.

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:26.533
Well done, Mr. Neelix.

00:13:37.683 --> 00:13:39.947
Commander Chakotay says
you've found something.

00:13:40.019 --> 00:13:42.214
That, Captain,
is an understatement.

00:13:42.288 --> 00:13:43.949
Listen.

00:13:45.324 --> 00:13:46.382
What is it?

00:13:46.458 --> 00:13:49.427
The sound of history being made.

00:13:49.495 --> 00:13:51.622
Less poetry, Mr. Naroq,
more facts.

00:13:51.697 --> 00:13:52.959
The sound you're hearing

00:13:53.032 --> 00:13:55.262
indicates the presence
of veridium isotopes.

00:13:55.334 --> 00:13:57.666
Residual particles from the
Ba'Neths' cloaking field.

00:13:57.736 --> 00:13:59.431
You've detected
these isotopes before?

00:13:59.505 --> 00:14:01.973
Yes, but only
after they've decayed.

00:14:02.041 --> 00:14:04.271
You see, veridium has
a very brief half-life...

00:14:04.343 --> 00:14:05.435
less than 70 hours.

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:07.274
The previous sites I've studied

00:14:07.346 --> 00:14:09.507
have been months,
sometimes years old!

00:14:09.582 --> 00:14:11.379
But these isotopes
are still active.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.645
We can use Mr. Naroq's
photolitic converter

00:14:13.719 --> 00:14:15.482
to illuminate them.

00:14:15.554 --> 00:14:18.216
So you see, Captain,
why this is an historic moment?

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.621
We may finally learn

00:14:19.692 --> 00:14:21.523
what the Ba'Neth look like.

00:14:21.594 --> 00:14:23.494
Well, let's see what we've got.

00:14:31.103 --> 00:14:33.936
You don't know how long
I've waited to meet you.

00:14:34.006 --> 00:14:36.941
So, the Ba'Neth aren't a myth
after all.

00:14:37.076 --> 00:14:38.941
This is the clearest image
ever captured!

00:14:39.078 --> 00:14:40.306
Perhaps.

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:43.314
I believe I can adjust our
internal sensors to improve it.

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:44.542
What are you doing?
What are you...

00:14:44.617 --> 00:14:46.915
You might disrupt
the image entirely.

00:14:52.124 --> 00:14:53.386
Tentacles!

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:56.189
I always suspected
they were multipeds.

00:14:56.262 --> 00:14:57.957
Doctor to the Captain.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.964
Please report to Sick Bay.

00:15:00.032 --> 00:15:01.795
I'm on my way.

00:15:01.867 --> 00:15:02.993
Seven...

00:15:03.068 --> 00:15:04.330
if we can integrate

00:15:04.403 --> 00:15:05.893
Mr. Naroq's
photolitic technology

00:15:06.005 --> 00:15:07.199
into the deflector array,

00:15:07.273 --> 00:15:09.366
we might be able to de-cloak
a Ba'Neth ship.

00:15:09.441 --> 00:15:12.376
The technology only works
at close range.

00:15:12.444 --> 00:15:15.208
We have to find the ship
before we can expose it.

00:15:15.281 --> 00:15:17.613
We still need
that cloaking frequency.

00:15:17.683 --> 00:15:19.310
One step at a time.

00:15:23.088 --> 00:15:24.578
The Vulcan brain...

00:15:24.657 --> 00:15:27.091
a puzzle
wrapped inside an enigma,

00:15:27.159 --> 00:15:28.820
housed inside a cranium.

00:15:28.894 --> 00:15:30.225
Tuvok's neural pathways

00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:32.196
have begun to bypass
the damaged tissue.

00:15:32.264 --> 00:15:33.925
They're forming
new synaptic connections.

00:15:33.999 --> 00:15:36.160
In effect, his brain
is rewiring itself.

00:15:36.235 --> 00:15:38.396
Whether this is due
to my neurostatic therapy

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:40.938
or Neelix's
rehabilitation regimen

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.940
or some combination of the two,
I can't be certain.

00:15:43.075 --> 00:15:45.202
Is there any chance he'll
make a full recovery?

00:15:45.277 --> 00:15:46.676
It's much too soon to say,

00:15:46.745 --> 00:15:48.804
but he's alert
and he's already regained

00:15:48.881 --> 00:15:50.644
his basic motor skills.

00:15:50.716 --> 00:15:51.944
But still no speech.

00:15:52.051 --> 00:15:54.178
It's only a matter of time,
Captain.

00:15:54.253 --> 00:15:56.050
Look how far he's come already.

00:15:56.121 --> 00:15:57.850
I hope you're right, Neelix.

00:15:57.923 --> 00:15:59.220
But if he could talk,
he might be able

00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:01.953
to tell us something
about that cloaking frequency.

00:16:02.027 --> 00:16:04.621
We're not sure
how much he recalls.

00:16:04.697 --> 00:16:06.028
For that matter,
we're not certain

00:16:06.098 --> 00:16:10.091
he recognizes any of us
or even knows who he is.

00:16:10.169 --> 00:16:12.865
I'm going to take him
on a tour of the ship.

00:16:12.938 --> 00:16:15.338
The Doctor thinks that familiar
sights and sounds

00:16:15.407 --> 00:16:18.069
might get the old
synaptic juices flowing.

00:16:21.914 --> 00:16:23.245
Don't worry, Captain.

00:16:23.315 --> 00:16:24.907
Tuvok will be back
to his old self

00:16:25.017 --> 00:16:27.281
before you can say,
"live long and prosper."

00:16:39.164 --> 00:16:40.597
I've brought a visitor.

00:16:40.666 --> 00:16:43.100
Good to see you up and around.

00:16:44.703 --> 00:16:46.830
You remember Commander Chakotay.

00:16:53.045 --> 00:16:55.479
We were just running
a shield diagnostic.

00:16:55.547 --> 00:16:57.481
Would you like to take a look?

00:16:57.549 --> 00:17:00.677
This is Tactical Station,
where you work.

00:17:06.992 --> 00:17:08.892
Just keeping it warm for you.

00:17:08.994 --> 00:17:10.962
Hope you don't mind.

00:17:14.233 --> 00:17:15.894
That's the shield array.

00:17:15.968 --> 00:17:18.300
This controls
the tractor emitters.

00:17:19.371 --> 00:17:21.498
I think he remembers it.

00:17:21.573 --> 00:17:23.302
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:17:25.077 --> 00:17:28.240
You just activated
the photon torpedo banks.

00:17:28.313 --> 00:17:29.905
That's all right, Tuvok.

00:17:30.015 --> 00:17:31.915
Everybody makes mistakes.

00:17:33.619 --> 00:17:35.678
We'll be back later.

00:17:46.031 --> 00:17:49.091
Last... but not least...

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:52.560
your quarters.

00:17:54.706 --> 00:17:57.368
You spend a lot of time here,

00:17:57.443 --> 00:17:59.240
reading...

00:17:59.311 --> 00:18:00.744
meditating...

00:18:03.315 --> 00:18:07.149
Mr. Paris once referred to it
as the "Vulcan Vault."

00:18:10.389 --> 00:18:12.186
Ahh...

00:18:12.257 --> 00:18:14.953
Well, look around, explore.

00:18:17.796 --> 00:18:19.457
Astrometrics to the Bridge.

00:18:19.531 --> 00:18:22.557
Mr. Naroq and I have completed
our deflector modifications.

00:18:22.634 --> 00:18:24.192
We're ready to test the array.

00:18:24.269 --> 00:18:25.361
Stand by.

00:18:25.437 --> 00:18:27.132
Reduce speed
to one-quarter impulse.

00:18:27.206 --> 00:18:29.197
Harry, full power
to the deflector array.

00:18:29.274 --> 00:18:30.866
Aye.

00:18:30.943 --> 00:18:33.776
All right, Seven...
do it.

00:18:33.846 --> 00:18:36.337
Activating the deflector.

00:18:39.351 --> 00:18:43.014
I'd call that
a pretty successful test.

00:18:43.088 --> 00:18:45.022
They've been watching us
all along.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.523
Hail them.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.359
Which one?

00:18:49.428 --> 00:18:51.020
There's practically
a fleet out there.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.863
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:18:56.935 --> 00:18:58.926
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:18:59.004 --> 00:19:00.835
We intend you no harm.

00:19:00.906 --> 00:19:02.339
They're charging weapons.

00:19:02.407 --> 00:19:03.567
Shields.

00:19:04.643 --> 00:19:06.406
They're scrambling, Captain,

00:19:06.478 --> 00:19:07.672
in all directions.

00:19:07.746 --> 00:19:09.611
Follow the lead vessel.

00:19:17.289 --> 00:19:19.154
It's okay, Tuvok.

00:19:19.224 --> 00:19:20.714
I'm here with you.

00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:23.852
Everything is going
to be all right.

00:19:26.231 --> 00:19:28.324
You're safe with me.

00:19:31.303 --> 00:19:32.930
Still no response to our hails.

00:19:34.506 --> 00:19:36.030
I hate to ruin a good chase,

00:19:36.108 --> 00:19:39.077
but the Ba'Neth ship is moving
out of the deflector's range.

00:19:39.144 --> 00:19:42.079
Seven, can you get
their cloaking frequency?

00:19:42.147 --> 00:19:43.774
They're blocking our scans.

00:19:43.849 --> 00:19:44.838
We've lost them.

00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:51.349
They're gone now, Tuvok.

00:19:56.528 --> 00:19:58.428
I told you you'd be safe.

00:19:59.998 --> 00:20:02.193
Yes...

00:20:02.267 --> 00:20:03.791
you did.

00:20:06.505 --> 00:20:07.995
Tuvok?

00:20:13.212 --> 00:20:14.372
What?

00:20:15.581 --> 00:20:18.516
Tell me, what did I do?

00:20:18.584 --> 00:20:21.178
You told me...

00:20:21.253 --> 00:20:23.983
I wouldn't be hurt.

00:20:29.027 --> 00:20:31.154
Do you know who I am?

00:20:33.298 --> 00:20:34.560
You are Neelix.

00:20:36.101 --> 00:20:38.797
I'm safe... with you.

00:20:50.048 --> 00:20:51.606
We need Tuvok to tell us

00:20:51.683 --> 00:20:54.208
anything he can remember
about the attack.

00:20:54.286 --> 00:20:56.584
Captain, he may be
talking again,

00:20:56.655 --> 00:20:58.987
but that doesn't mean
he's ready

00:20:59.091 --> 00:21:00.251
to be interrogated.

00:21:00.325 --> 00:21:02.259
He's beginning
to experience emotions...

00:21:02.327 --> 00:21:03.521
volatile ones.

00:21:03.595 --> 00:21:06.689
During this last encounter with
the Ba'Neth, he was terrified.

00:21:06.765 --> 00:21:08.733
We'll tread lightly,
I promise.

00:21:11.003 --> 00:21:14.439
All right, Tuvok,
you can come in now.

00:21:19.511 --> 00:21:21.843
It's nice to see you.

00:21:24.049 --> 00:21:25.414
Captain Janeway.

00:21:25.484 --> 00:21:26.576
That's right.

00:21:26.652 --> 00:21:28.620
This is Mr. Naroq.

00:21:28.687 --> 00:21:30.279
Please sit down.

00:21:30.355 --> 00:21:33.324
Two days ago, you
were aboard a shuttle

00:21:33.392 --> 00:21:34.620
with Mr. Neelix.

00:21:34.693 --> 00:21:36.888
You detected a cloaked intruder.

00:21:36.962 --> 00:21:38.554
He attacked you.

00:21:40.198 --> 00:21:41.563
Yes...

00:21:41.633 --> 00:21:44.101
th-that's why I'm having
difficulty now.

00:21:44.169 --> 00:21:46.262
Yes, and in order to help you,

00:21:46.338 --> 00:21:49.330
we have to find
the people who hurt you.

00:21:49.408 --> 00:21:51.603
Before the intruder injured you,

00:21:51.677 --> 00:21:54.111
you managed to scan
him with this.

00:21:54.179 --> 00:21:56.909
You recorded
his cloaking frequency,

00:21:56.982 --> 00:22:01.078
but the tricorder was damaged
and the information was lost.

00:22:01.153 --> 00:22:04.054
Can you tell us anything
about that frequency?

00:22:04.122 --> 00:22:05.419
Try to remember.

00:22:11.263 --> 00:22:12.890
I was scanning.

00:22:12.964 --> 00:22:13.931
That's right.

00:22:14.066 --> 00:22:15.624
What did you see?

00:22:23.475 --> 00:22:25.340
I... I don't remember.

00:22:25.410 --> 00:22:26.434
Try!

00:22:26.511 --> 00:22:28.604
All right, that's enough.

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:29.578
We're done for now.

00:22:29.648 --> 00:22:30.910
But, Captain...

00:22:30.982 --> 00:22:32.506
Join Seven of Nine
in Astrometrics.

00:22:32.584 --> 00:22:34.882
See if she's made any progress
with the Ba'Neth.

00:22:37.622 --> 00:22:39.453
Well, uh, we should
be going, too.

00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:41.651
A few of the crew
have offered to help

00:22:41.727 --> 00:22:43.285
with Tuvok's rehabilitation.

00:22:43.362 --> 00:22:46.297
I thought we might have lunch
later, just the two of us.

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:50.666
I prefer to stay with Neelix.

00:22:50.736 --> 00:22:53.261
Oh, Tuvok... I'm-I'm sure
that you would...

00:22:53.338 --> 00:22:54.305
It's all right.

00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:55.567
You two go ahead.

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:57.904
I have a lot of work
to do anyway.

00:22:57.976 --> 00:22:58.943
Oh...

00:23:06.184 --> 00:23:07.776
The object of the game

00:23:07.853 --> 00:23:11.186
is to turn this jumble of rods
into a perfect sphere.

00:23:11.256 --> 00:23:13.690
We take turns
positioning our pieces.

00:23:13.759 --> 00:23:16.694
Whoever gets the shape
to appear first wins.

00:23:16.762 --> 00:23:19.162
I like the way it looks now.

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:24.601
What do you say
we give it a try?

00:23:24.669 --> 00:23:28.070
This has always been one
of your favorite games, Tuvok.

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:31.769
It helps keep your logic sharp.

00:23:31.843 --> 00:23:33.242
I'll go first.

00:23:42.087 --> 00:23:42.951
Now you.

00:23:43.088 --> 00:23:44.988
Go ahead.

00:24:06.978 --> 00:24:09.173
I don't like this game.

00:24:09.247 --> 00:24:11.511
When you first taught me
how to play,

00:24:11.583 --> 00:24:12.914
I wasn't very good, either,

00:24:12.984 --> 00:24:14.451
but you kept encouraging me

00:24:14.519 --> 00:24:16.817
and pretty soon,
I scored my first kal-toh.

00:24:16.888 --> 00:24:19.686
It just takes
practice, that's all.

00:24:19.758 --> 00:24:20.747
Try again.

00:24:20.826 --> 00:24:22.088
You can do it.

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:24.253
I don't like this game!

00:24:35.674 --> 00:24:39.075
The Doctor helped me access
my personnel file.

00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:43.738
Nice picture.

00:24:43.815 --> 00:24:45.282
You should see mine.

00:24:45.350 --> 00:24:47.147
It's awful.

00:24:47.219 --> 00:24:51.952
I was an instructor
at Starfleet Academy.

00:24:52.023 --> 00:24:56.221
I've received
17 commendations for valor.

00:24:56.294 --> 00:24:58.626
I'm a husband...

00:24:58.697 --> 00:25:00.631
a father.

00:25:00.699 --> 00:25:03.532
You're an extraordinary fellow,
Tuvok.

00:25:03.602 --> 00:25:07.868
I was an extraordinary fellow.

00:25:07.939 --> 00:25:10.271
You're still the same person.

00:25:12.711 --> 00:25:15.578
Then why do I no longer work
on the Bridge?

00:25:15.647 --> 00:25:18.582
We talked about that.

00:25:18.650 --> 00:25:20.880
You had an accident.

00:25:20.952 --> 00:25:23.216
And now I'm not smart enough.

00:25:25.123 --> 00:25:27.717
Tuvok, you've just
got to be patient.

00:25:27.792 --> 00:25:31.159
Look how much progress
you've made already.

00:25:31.229 --> 00:25:34.858
He... could dismantle
a photonic warhead

00:25:34.933 --> 00:25:37.561
in... in less than 30 seconds.

00:25:37.636 --> 00:25:40.230
I can't even play kal-toh.

00:25:40.305 --> 00:25:41.932
It's going to take time,

00:25:42.073 --> 00:25:44.837
but you'll relearn
all those things.

00:25:44.910 --> 00:25:46.810
How do you know that?

00:25:46.878 --> 00:25:48.436
Well, because the Doctor...

00:25:48.513 --> 00:25:49.844
The Doctor?

00:25:49.915 --> 00:25:52.110
The Doctor doesn't know
how to make me better!

00:25:52.183 --> 00:25:53.480
Does he?

00:25:53.552 --> 00:25:55.383
Well, not yet, but...

00:25:55.453 --> 00:25:57.785
I'll never be him again!

00:25:57.856 --> 00:25:59.824
You don't know that.

00:25:59.891 --> 00:26:01.119
The Vulcan mind...

00:26:01.192 --> 00:26:02.659
I'm not a Vulcan!

00:26:02.727 --> 00:26:03.751
Not anymore!

00:26:07.232 --> 00:26:08.722
What's going on?

00:26:08.800 --> 00:26:09.824
It's okay, Doctor.

00:26:09.901 --> 00:26:10.993
I can handle this.

00:26:11.069 --> 00:26:13.060
Please, Tuvok, try to relax.

00:26:13.138 --> 00:26:15.504
Everything's going to be fine.

00:26:15.574 --> 00:26:16.905
No! Nothing's fine!

00:26:16.975 --> 00:26:18.374
Get away from me!

00:26:18.443 --> 00:26:19.432
You'd better go.

00:26:19.511 --> 00:26:20.842
Now, Mr. Neelix!

00:26:20.912 --> 00:26:22.573
I'll take it from here.

00:26:40.165 --> 00:26:42.326
Oh, sorry;
I didn't mean to interrupt.

00:26:42.400 --> 00:26:43.924
You didn't.

00:26:44.035 --> 00:26:46.503
Yes, I did.

00:26:46.571 --> 00:26:48.539
You were pondering...

00:26:48.607 --> 00:26:51.542
something difficult,
by the looks of it.

00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:54.170
Anything I can help you with?

00:26:54.245 --> 00:26:57.043
Unlikely.

00:26:57.115 --> 00:26:59.208
Try me.

00:27:04.889 --> 00:27:08.086
How do you find something
that's invisible?

00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:11.424
The Ba'Neth.

00:27:11.496 --> 00:27:13.157
We have the ability
to illuminate them,

00:27:13.231 --> 00:27:14.892
but to do so,
we must first locate them,

00:27:15.033 --> 00:27:16.398
which we cannot accomplish

00:27:16.468 --> 00:27:17.992
without their
cloaking frequency.

00:27:18.069 --> 00:27:20.833
That's quite a riddle.

00:27:20.905 --> 00:27:22.429
One that we might
be able to solve

00:27:22.507 --> 00:27:24.600
if Commander Tuvok could tell us
what he saw.

00:27:24.676 --> 00:27:28.510
How is his rehabilitation
progressing?

00:27:28.580 --> 00:27:34.348
Well, I thought
it was going great, but now...

00:27:34.419 --> 00:27:38.583
let's just say that I've got
a riddle of my own.

00:27:40.525 --> 00:27:42.925
Try me.

00:27:43.061 --> 00:27:45.188
All right.

00:27:45.263 --> 00:27:49.222
When is a Vulcan
no longer a Vulcan?

00:27:49.300 --> 00:27:53.202
When his genetic code
is sufficiently altered.

00:27:53.271 --> 00:27:55.398
No. I-I-I was speaking
metaphorically.

00:27:55.473 --> 00:27:58.374
In that case, a person
is no longer Vulcan

00:27:58.443 --> 00:28:00.138
when he's lost his logic.

00:28:00.211 --> 00:28:01.269
Right!

00:28:01.346 --> 00:28:02.870
And how does he get it back?

00:28:02.947 --> 00:28:04.209
He must be taught.

00:28:04.282 --> 00:28:07.115
Exactly, but what
if he's brain damaged

00:28:07.185 --> 00:28:09.016
and emotionally unstable?

00:28:09.087 --> 00:28:11.647
How does he learn?

00:28:11.723 --> 00:28:14.590
It may be impossible
for him to learn

00:28:14.659 --> 00:28:16.650
what you're trying to teach.

00:28:16.728 --> 00:28:18.787
Well, thanks for the pep talk.

00:28:18.863 --> 00:28:20.194
I was merely suggesting

00:28:20.265 --> 00:28:22.392
that you adapt
to the circumstances.

00:28:22.467 --> 00:28:23.866
What circumstances?!

00:28:23.935 --> 00:28:26.631
Are you saying that the,
the Tuvok I know is gone...

00:28:26.705 --> 00:28:28.673
that I should stop
trying to help him?

00:28:28.740 --> 00:28:30.901
When I was separated
from the collective,

00:28:31.009 --> 00:28:32.476
I, too, was damaged.

00:28:32.544 --> 00:28:34.409
I was no longer connected
to the hive mind.

00:28:34.479 --> 00:28:36.447
I lost many abilities

00:28:36.514 --> 00:28:39.745
that I had acquired as a drone,
but I adapted.

00:28:39.818 --> 00:28:43.219
Because Captain Janeway
didn't give up on you.

00:28:43.288 --> 00:28:45.916
She kept trying to help you.

00:28:45.990 --> 00:28:49.187
But not by restoring me
to what I'd been...

00:28:49.260 --> 00:28:52.627
by helping me discover
what I could become.

00:29:02.440 --> 00:29:05.204
What are you making?

00:29:05.276 --> 00:29:06.834
A flower.

00:29:14.285 --> 00:29:17.982
It's for you.

00:29:18.056 --> 00:29:19.546
Thank you.

00:29:19.624 --> 00:29:23.651
I'm not sure I deserve a gift.

00:29:23.728 --> 00:29:27.664
I shouldn't have shouted at you.

00:29:27.732 --> 00:29:29.131
I was angry.

00:29:29.200 --> 00:29:31.259
I'm sorry.

00:29:31.336 --> 00:29:32.894
You were frustrated.

00:29:33.004 --> 00:29:35.905
I don't blame you.

00:29:35.974 --> 00:29:38.033
I'm the one who
should be apologizing.

00:29:38.109 --> 00:29:39.508
Why?

00:29:39.577 --> 00:29:43.172
Because I was pushing
you too hard.

00:29:43.248 --> 00:29:48.083
I was trying to mold you
into something you weren't.

00:29:48.153 --> 00:29:50.553
You were disappointed in me

00:29:50.622 --> 00:29:53.682
because I can't
do anything as well

00:29:53.758 --> 00:29:54.782
as I did before.

00:29:54.859 --> 00:29:58.056
Maybe there are things
that you can do better.

00:29:58.129 --> 00:30:00.825
What can I do better?

00:30:00.899 --> 00:30:04.926
Well... this, for example.

00:30:05.036 --> 00:30:09.473
You would've considered it
an "illogical use of your time."

00:30:09.541 --> 00:30:11.566
It's not good.

00:30:11.643 --> 00:30:13.440
No, it's wonderful.

00:30:13.511 --> 00:30:15.308
It's... creative.

00:30:15.380 --> 00:30:17.678
It's a symbol of friendship.

00:30:17.749 --> 00:30:22.186
Before your accident,
you never would have considered

00:30:22.253 --> 00:30:24.187
that my feelings
might have been hurt.

00:30:24.255 --> 00:30:28.214
You, you would have certainly
never have made me a gift.

00:30:28.293 --> 00:30:31.160
We weren't friends?

00:30:31.229 --> 00:30:33.197
Well, uh...

00:30:33.264 --> 00:30:35.789
we were colleagues,

00:30:35.867 --> 00:30:39.826
and I certainly felt affection
for you.

00:30:42.607 --> 00:30:45.872
But I didn't return
those feelings.

00:30:45.944 --> 00:30:49.380
You... tolerated me.

00:30:49.447 --> 00:30:51.210
I don't understand.

00:30:51.282 --> 00:30:53.273
You said things like

00:30:53.351 --> 00:30:57.913
"Mr. Neelix, please contain
your exuberance."

00:30:57.989 --> 00:31:02.892
And, uh, "Mr. Neelix,
I have no desire for fun."

00:31:03.962 --> 00:31:05.190
And you never smiled.

00:31:05.263 --> 00:31:07.823
You got a much better
sense of humor now.

00:31:07.899 --> 00:31:09.332
I like to smile.

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:10.924
Me, too.

00:31:14.239 --> 00:31:16.571
I don't want to play
kal-toh anymore...

00:31:16.641 --> 00:31:18.370
or-or meditate...

00:31:18.443 --> 00:31:20.638
or... work on logic problems.

00:31:20.712 --> 00:31:22.236
You don't have to.

00:31:22.313 --> 00:31:24.406
What can we do instead?

00:31:24.482 --> 00:31:26.279
Whatever you want.

00:31:26.351 --> 00:31:29.411
Teach me things
that you like to do.

00:31:33.892 --> 00:31:34.950
Here we are...

00:31:35.093 --> 00:31:37.687
a triple-chocolate
wikki fruit sundae

00:31:37.762 --> 00:31:39.696
with warm fettran sauce.

00:31:39.764 --> 00:31:42.824
Fettran sauce on...
a sundae?

00:31:42.901 --> 00:31:44.493
Wait till you taste it.

00:31:44.569 --> 00:31:46.560
And you really made this?

00:31:46.638 --> 00:31:48.799
As Neelix says, dig in.

00:31:51.276 --> 00:31:53.904
Mmm... this is great.

00:31:53.978 --> 00:31:55.673
This is fantastic.

00:31:55.747 --> 00:31:57.612
What did I tell you?

00:31:57.682 --> 00:32:00.981
Tuvok has a flair for food.

00:32:01.052 --> 00:32:03.452
All morning, he's been
creating new recipes,

00:32:03.521 --> 00:32:05.580
using combinations
of ingredients

00:32:05.657 --> 00:32:07.625
that I, I never would
have imagined.

00:32:07.692 --> 00:32:08.659
For example...

00:32:08.726 --> 00:32:09.920
a terra nut soufflé...

00:32:10.061 --> 00:32:13.326
Jimbalian fudge cake
with peppermint coulis...

00:32:13.398 --> 00:32:15.832
sweet leola root tart.

00:32:15.900 --> 00:32:16.832
Mmm!

00:32:16.901 --> 00:32:18.630
Only desserts?
How come?

00:32:18.703 --> 00:32:20.068
They taste good.

00:32:20.138 --> 00:32:21.162
Ha!

00:32:21.239 --> 00:32:23.036
Yeah, you better
watch out, Neelix.

00:32:23.107 --> 00:32:24.699
Tuvok may put you out of a job.

00:32:24.776 --> 00:32:27.711
From your mouth
to the Captain's ears.

00:32:27.779 --> 00:32:28.939
She must have heard me.

00:32:30.315 --> 00:32:31.714
What's all this?

00:32:31.783 --> 00:32:33.808
We're having fun.

00:32:33.885 --> 00:32:36.945
Uh, turns out Tuvok is
quite the pastry chef.

00:32:37.088 --> 00:32:39.522
Would you like some
terra nut soufflé, Captain?

00:32:39.590 --> 00:32:40.955
Oh, I'd love some.

00:32:41.025 --> 00:32:43.255
Thank you.

00:32:43.328 --> 00:32:45.262
Oh...

00:32:45.330 --> 00:32:47.093
that is delicious.

00:32:47.165 --> 00:32:49.360
I'm pleased that you like it.

00:32:55.306 --> 00:32:57.501
What are you making now?

00:32:57.575 --> 00:33:00.908
Pistachio cake
with parra cream sauce.

00:33:00.979 --> 00:33:02.708
Oh, parra cream's my favorite.

00:33:02.780 --> 00:33:05.476
Then you'll have
the first piece.

00:33:05.550 --> 00:33:08.451
Tuvok, have you
remembered anything more

00:33:08.519 --> 00:33:10.288
about what happened
on the Flyer?

00:33:15.493 --> 00:33:18.792
I detected a cloaking frequency.

00:33:18.863 --> 00:33:20.592
Yes, that's right.

00:33:20.665 --> 00:33:23.429
Can you describe it?

00:33:28.639 --> 00:33:30.903
I don't know, I, I...

00:33:30.975 --> 00:33:33.569
Did it have
a symmetric modulation?

00:33:33.644 --> 00:33:36.204
Was the amplitude constant?

00:33:36.280 --> 00:33:37.474
I-I don't understand.

00:33:37.548 --> 00:33:38.480
It's all right.

00:33:38.549 --> 00:33:40.574
I don't mean to push you, Tuvok,

00:33:40.651 --> 00:33:41.948
but maybe if we could...

00:33:42.020 --> 00:33:43.954
It's difficult for him,
Captain.

00:33:44.088 --> 00:33:46.818
Maybe you can try again
tomorrow.

00:33:46.891 --> 00:33:48.916
This...

00:33:54.499 --> 00:33:56.467
This is what I saw.

00:33:56.534 --> 00:33:57.967
What is it?

00:34:01.606 --> 00:34:03.506
A cloaking frequency.

00:34:06.010 --> 00:34:07.568
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:34:07.645 --> 00:34:09.875
The computer has analyzed
Tuvok's diagram

00:34:09.947 --> 00:34:12.472
and identified
the Ba'Neth cloaking frequency.

00:34:12.550 --> 00:34:15.576
We've narrowed the search
to a handful of systems.

00:34:15.653 --> 00:34:17.211
Here we go, Captain.

00:34:17.288 --> 00:34:20.223
A nine-million terawatt
cloaking field in Grid 216.

00:34:20.291 --> 00:34:21.918
Nine million terawatts.

00:34:22.026 --> 00:34:23.618
Whatever they're hiding,
it's huge.

00:34:23.694 --> 00:34:25.252
Alter course, Mr. Paris.

00:34:25.329 --> 00:34:26.523
Yes, ma'am.

00:34:26.597 --> 00:34:28.394
Bridge to Astrometrics.
Status.

00:34:28.466 --> 00:34:31.026
The deflector array
is ready, Captain.

00:34:31.102 --> 00:34:32.865
Raise shields.

00:34:32.937 --> 00:34:34.063
Aye, Captain.

00:34:34.138 --> 00:34:35.833
We're within range.

00:34:35.907 --> 00:34:37.602
All right, Seven...

00:34:37.675 --> 00:34:39.404
light them up.

00:34:49.887 --> 00:34:52.947
It's an armed outpost.

00:34:53.024 --> 00:34:55.185
Approximately
3,000 life signs, 22 ships.

00:34:55.259 --> 00:34:56.226
Hail them.

00:34:58.262 --> 00:34:59.456
No response, Captain.

00:34:59.530 --> 00:35:00.861
They're charging weapons.

00:35:00.932 --> 00:35:03.230
Open a channel,
all subspace bands.

00:35:04.335 --> 00:35:05.632
They're firing.

00:35:05.703 --> 00:35:08.763
Cease fire immediately...

00:35:08.840 --> 00:35:10.307
or I'll transmit

00:35:10.374 --> 00:35:14.538
the coordinates of this outpost
to the Kesat homeworld.

00:35:16.180 --> 00:35:19.274
That got their attention.

00:35:19.350 --> 00:35:20.783
Several days ago,

00:35:20.852 --> 00:35:23.514
a member of your species
attacked one of my crewmen.

00:35:23.588 --> 00:35:24.919
He was badly injured.

00:35:25.056 --> 00:35:26.648
In order to treat him,

00:35:26.724 --> 00:35:29.386
I need to know more
about the weapon that was used.

00:35:29.460 --> 00:35:30.484
They're responding.

00:35:30.561 --> 00:35:31.493
Audio only.

00:35:31.562 --> 00:35:34.588
We do not share technology.

00:35:34.665 --> 00:35:36.496
But you take it from others.

00:35:36.567 --> 00:35:39.934
The attacker was downloading
our tactical database

00:35:40.004 --> 00:35:41.835
when the incident occurred.

00:35:41.906 --> 00:35:44.101
We must assess
potential threats.

00:35:44.175 --> 00:35:46.166
Paranoid, just as I predicted.

00:35:46.244 --> 00:35:49.338
In exchange for information
about your weapon,

00:35:49.413 --> 00:35:51.938
we'll provide you
with tactical data

00:35:52.049 --> 00:35:55.280
on several species
we've recently encountered.

00:35:55.353 --> 00:35:59.119
You can assess their
potential threats all you want.

00:35:59.190 --> 00:36:03.854
The Kesat investigator aboard
your vessel cannot be trusted.

00:36:05.263 --> 00:36:07.026
You know about me?

00:36:07.098 --> 00:36:09.896
You have been attempting
to expose us for years.

00:36:10.001 --> 00:36:11.798
You are a threat.

00:36:11.869 --> 00:36:14.099
You must be stopped.

00:36:14.172 --> 00:36:15.764
They're charging weapons again.

00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:17.000
Wait.

00:36:17.074 --> 00:36:19.542
It was my photolitic converter

00:36:19.610 --> 00:36:22.636
that allowed Voyager
to de-cloak you.

00:36:22.713 --> 00:36:26.342
If you give Captain Janeway
what she wants,

00:36:26.417 --> 00:36:28.385
I'll give you the converter.

00:36:28.452 --> 00:36:31.444
You can use it
to adapt your technology

00:36:31.522 --> 00:36:33.490
so ours can no longer
expose you.

00:36:36.194 --> 00:36:38.685
I doubt you'll get
as enticing an offer

00:36:38.763 --> 00:36:40.458
from the Kesat homeworld.

00:36:40.531 --> 00:36:44.991
It would be a shame
if you forced me to hail them.

00:36:48.005 --> 00:36:49.302
We have an agreement.

00:36:57.582 --> 00:36:58.549
Enter.

00:37:01.052 --> 00:37:02.986
What are you listening to?

00:37:03.054 --> 00:37:06.114
A selection
from Tom's jazz database...

00:37:06.190 --> 00:37:08.920
it really swings.

00:37:11.162 --> 00:37:14.029
Computer, pause the music.

00:37:14.098 --> 00:37:18.194
I've been reviewing
the holodeck files.

00:37:18.269 --> 00:37:21.238
I wish to visit the Risa
Water Recreation Park.

00:37:21.305 --> 00:37:22.795
Will you accompany me?

00:37:22.873 --> 00:37:25.205
Maybe after
your doctor's appointment.

00:37:25.276 --> 00:37:26.709
Appointment?

00:37:26.777 --> 00:37:30.144
The Doctor's analyzed
the Ba'Neth weapon,

00:37:30.214 --> 00:37:33.741
and he's devised
a procedure to treat you.

00:37:40.224 --> 00:37:44.923
You... you should be
proud of yourself.

00:37:45.062 --> 00:37:47.553
L-if you hadn't drawn
that picture on the cake,

00:37:47.632 --> 00:37:49.395
we may never have found
a treatment.

00:37:51.369 --> 00:37:53.769
I wish I never drew
that picture.

00:37:53.838 --> 00:37:55.897
Why?

00:37:58.175 --> 00:38:02.271
Because I don't wish
to undergo the procedure.

00:38:02.346 --> 00:38:05.076
You're having
preoperative jitters.

00:38:05.149 --> 00:38:06.081
That's all.

00:38:06.150 --> 00:38:07.117
Don't worry.

00:38:07.184 --> 00:38:09.015
Everyone gets them.

00:38:09.086 --> 00:38:10.713
Just think about it.

00:38:10.788 --> 00:38:13.154
In a few hours,
you'll be yourself again.

00:38:13.224 --> 00:38:15.988
I am myself.

00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:19.188
But... you'll be able
to do all the things

00:38:19.263 --> 00:38:20.855
that you used to do...

00:38:20.931 --> 00:38:22.330
work on the Bridge,

00:38:22.400 --> 00:38:23.731
advise the Captain.

00:38:23.801 --> 00:38:25.826
I want to be able to have fun.

00:38:25.903 --> 00:38:28.371
With you.

00:38:30.675 --> 00:38:32.802
I won't be able to.

00:38:32.877 --> 00:38:34.310
Will I?

00:38:34.378 --> 00:38:36.539
Well...

00:38:41.952 --> 00:38:44.079
you won't call it fun.

00:38:44.155 --> 00:38:47.613
You'll call it
"deriving satisfaction,"

00:38:47.692 --> 00:38:50.661
but it's basically
the same thing.

00:38:50.728 --> 00:38:53.128
You'll still
experience emotions.

00:38:53.197 --> 00:38:56.689
But I won't express them.

00:38:56.767 --> 00:38:59.964
Probably not.

00:39:04.842 --> 00:39:10.303
Then how will you know
how much I enjoy being with you?

00:39:11.916 --> 00:39:14.384
You've just told me.

00:39:17.421 --> 00:39:19.787
We'll still be friends?

00:39:19.857 --> 00:39:22.553
Of course.

00:39:22.626 --> 00:39:28.496
Even if I...
merely tolerate you?

00:39:28.566 --> 00:39:31.763
I'd be lying if I told you

00:39:31.836 --> 00:39:33.861
that things between us
will stay the same.

00:39:36.307 --> 00:39:37.899
Well, then, why?

00:39:38.042 --> 00:39:40.806
Why do you want me to go back
to the way I was?

00:39:45.916 --> 00:39:48.043
Because this crew needs

00:39:48.119 --> 00:39:51.179
its Tactical Officer
on the Bridge,

00:39:51.255 --> 00:39:54.520
and I wouldn't be
a very good friend

00:39:54.592 --> 00:39:59.029
if I ignored that just
so that you'd be nicer to me.

00:40:06.103 --> 00:40:09.766
Mr. Tuvok, I was beginning
to think you weren't coming.

00:40:09.840 --> 00:40:14.277
I was experiencing
preoperative jitters.

00:40:14.345 --> 00:40:16.370
Neelix helped me overcome them.

00:40:16.447 --> 00:40:18.347
Glad to hear it.

00:40:18.416 --> 00:40:20.782
Now, please lie down.

00:40:28.859 --> 00:40:31.225
I'll see you
after the procedure?

00:40:31.295 --> 00:40:34.128
Of course.

00:40:40.871 --> 00:40:43.567
I'm going to miss him.

00:40:43.641 --> 00:40:45.973
Me, too.

00:41:22.980 --> 00:41:24.948
Hello, Commander.

00:41:25.015 --> 00:41:26.380
Mr. Neelix.

00:41:30.187 --> 00:41:33.520
It's good to see
you up and about.

00:41:33.591 --> 00:41:35.957
Are you feeling better?

00:41:36.060 --> 00:41:39.154
The Doctor has approved
my return to duty.

00:41:39.230 --> 00:41:41.061
That's wonderful news.

00:41:41.131 --> 00:41:44.589
How about a celebratory
glass of champagne?

00:41:44.668 --> 00:41:47.034
Tea will suffice.

00:41:48.239 --> 00:41:49.934
Of course.

00:41:56.914 --> 00:41:59.246
I'm preparing
a special dinner tonight,

00:41:59.316 --> 00:42:01.011
in honor of your recovery.

00:42:03.220 --> 00:42:06.348
I don't suppose
that you'd be interested

00:42:06.423 --> 00:42:09.517
in preparing one
of your famous desserts.

00:42:09.593 --> 00:42:11.561
I have much more important
things to do

00:42:11.629 --> 00:42:13.290
than engage in the preparation

00:42:13.364 --> 00:42:15.025
of nutritionally
deficient foods.

00:42:17.234 --> 00:42:20.931
Maybe another time.

00:42:21.071 --> 00:42:22.868
Sundays.

00:42:22.940 --> 00:42:25.135
I beg your pardon?

00:42:25.209 --> 00:42:26.836
I have given
further consideration

00:42:26.911 --> 00:42:30.074
to your riddle regarding
the Ensign who survived

00:42:30.147 --> 00:42:32.809
by consuming the "dates"
from his calendar.

00:42:32.883 --> 00:42:34.373
It occurs to me

00:42:34.451 --> 00:42:38.353
that he could also have eaten
the "Sundays."

00:42:41.592 --> 00:42:43.890
That's a very clever answer,
Mr. Vulcan.

00:42:47.765 --> 00:42:50.256
But it's not very logical,
is it?

00:42:54.305 --> 00:42:56.535
No.

00:42:56.607 --> 00:42:58.074
It's not.
